## Commands

Commands are shown for this repo's package manager (`{{run}} …`).

```bash
{{run}} verify         # the whole local gate set in CI order (run before pushing)
{{run}} dev            # watch build; deploys into $OBSIDIAN_VAULT (hot reload)
{{run}} build          # production bundle (main.js + styles.css)
{{run}} test           # Vitest (jsdom; obsidian aliased to tests/__mocks__/obsidian.ts){{coverageLine}}
{{run}} typecheck      # {{typecheckTool}} --noEmit
{{run}} format         # prettier --write{{lintLine}}{{locLine}}{{cssLine}}{{qualityLine}}
{{run}} check:artifacts # post-build artifact smoke (run after build)
```

## Development notes

- **Obsidian-native first**: build DOM with `createEl`/`createDiv`/`createSpan`/
  `setText`/`.empty()`; render markdown through `MarkdownRenderer`. Raw HTML
  sinks (`innerHTML`/`outerHTML`/`insertAdjacentHTML`) are lint-banned (XSS).
- No `console.*` in production code (lint-enforced); UI copy is sentence case.
- User feedback goes through `plugin.notices` / `plugin.modals` — raw
  `new Notice()` outside NoticeService is lint-banned.
- Register commands via `plugin.commands` in `src/commands.ts`
  (`addSimple`/`addChecked`/`addEditor`); keep `main.ts` orchestration-only.
- {{mobileLine}}
- {{vueLine}}
- Style with Obsidian CSS variables in `src/styles.css`; avoid `!important`
  (ratcheted by `check:css`).
- **TDD workflow**: for new behavior or bug fixes, write the failing test first
  under `tests/`, make it pass, then refactor.
- Ratchets (`check:loc`, `check:css`, `check:quality`, coverage floors) may
  improve but never regress; lock improvements in with each gate's `--update`
  in the same PR.
- Run `{{run}} verify` before pushing.

